  "updatedAt": "2026-03-05T20:29:45.657Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef positional_encoding(seq_len: int, d_model: int, base: float = 10000.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    pe = np.zeros((seq_len, d_model), dtype=float)\n    pos = np.arange(seq_len)[:, np.newaxis]\n    i_idx = np.arange(0, d_model, 2)\n    div = np.exp(i_idx * (-math.log(base) / d_model))\n    pe[:, 0::2] = np.sin(pos * div)\n    cos_cols = d_model // 2\n    pe[:, 1::2] = np.cos(pos * div[:cos_cols])\n    return np.round(pe, 4)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
